---
/**
 * An accessibility statement is only worth having if it is honest, so this one
 * names what the site actually does rather than claiming conformance it has
 * not been audited for. "Aiming for WCAG 2.1 AA" is a commitment; "conforms to
 * WCAG 2.1 AA" would be a claim nobody here has tested.
 *
 * The audience matters more than usual: this site is read by older adults and
 * by family members who may be tired, on a phone, and in a hurry. The offer to
 * do by phone anything the site can do is the substantive part of this page.
 *
 * NOT REVIEWED BY COUNSEL, and not audited by an accessibility specialist.
 */

// COMPONENTS
import LegalPage from "@/components/LegalPage.astro";

// DATA
import { baseData, telHref, mailHref } from "@/data/siteData";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Accessibility"
  updated="September 8, 2026"
  pageTitle={`Accessibility | ${baseData.title}`}
  description="Our commitment to keeping the Quantum Home Cares website usable for everyone, and how to tell us when it is not."
>
  <p class="lead">
    Most people who read this site are arranging care for someone they love, often at a hard moment.
    It should not be hard to use. {baseData.legalName} is committed to keeping this website usable for
    everyone, including people who browse with assistive technology.
  </p>

  <h2>What we are aiming for</h2>

  <p>
    We build toward the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines, version 2.1, at conformance level AA.
    That is the standard most widely referenced for public websites. We have not had this site
    independently audited, so we describe this as the target we work to rather than a certification
    we hold.
  </p>

  <h2>What we have done</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Every page can be navigated by keyboard, and focus is visible as you move through it.</li>
    <li>Headings run in order, so a screen reader can move through a page by structure.</li>
    <li>
      Images that carry meaning have text descriptions; decorative ones are hidden from screen
      readers.
    </li>
    <li>Body text and interface colors are chosen for contrast against their backgrounds.</li>
    <li>Text reflows down to small screens and stays readable when you zoom in.</li>
    <li>Motion and animation are reduced automatically if your device asks for that.</li>
    <li>Forms use real labels, and errors are announced rather than shown by color alone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where we know we fall short</h2>

  <p>
    Accessibility is ongoing work, not a box to tick. Some content on this site comes from outside
    services, including our feedback widget and any embedded material, and we do not control how
    accessible those are. If you hit a barrier anywhere, we would rather hear about it than not.
  </p>

  <h2>You never have to use the website</h2>

  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Anything the site can do, a phone call can do.</strong> If a form is difficult to use, or
      a page will not work with your software, call <a href={telHref}>{baseData.phone}</a> and we will
      take your request, answer your questions, or read you anything on the site. There is no part of
      arranging care that requires you to fill in a form.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Telling us about a problem</h2>

  <p>
    If something on this site is hard to use, contact us at <a href={mailHref}>{baseData.email}</a> or
    <a href={telHref}>{baseData.phone}</a>. It helps if you can tell us the page, what you were
    trying to do, and what browser or assistive technology you were using, but tell us anyway even
    if you cannot.
  </p>

  <p>
    We aim to respond within one business day and to fix what we can fix quickly. Where a fix will
    take longer, we will tell you and offer another way to get what you needed.
  </p>

  <p>{baseData.legalName} · {baseData.credentials.license}</p>
</LegalPage>
